sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Danio nigrofasciatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 27 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 75.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics at a=0.1, b=0.9, D_u=0.05, D_v=2.0 so that lambda_c = 2.71e-05 m (27 µm, log10=-4.567, tier 4_cellular_10um) at geological age 0 Ma. One-step eigenmode growth matches analytical sigma(k) at Pearson r = 0.999997 (RMSE 0.00141). The trunk of the Parichy CC BY 4.0 photograph is the render scaffold. Full credit for the alpha sweep, KS holdout, and ablation is withheld until Pass 2 re-runs them. Overall 75.9/100 (faithfulness 73.1, reproducibility 82.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8585ec4a033d94afd4c400aaefdffe79c1f7bc69; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 66, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 76, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/danio_nigrofasciatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8585ec4a033d94afd4c400aaefdffe79c1f7bc69, image/png, 844084 B, 1344×960 px, artifact_sha256 148886b92b1be1b13cf7f30fa6946f8dd7aac8ca06dca5c43b6ee09787de9e5d (sha256 148886b92b1be1b13cf7f30fa6946f8dd7aac8ca06dca5c43b6ee09787de9e5d), spec_fingerprint 91717ca6df274e3e1c0bf367643f453836a534d386c3a9a413fc1a38ae61dfdd. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 91717ca6df274e3e1c0bf367643f453836a534d386c3a9a413fc1a38ae61dfdd; artifact_sha256: 148886b92b1be1b13cf7f30fa6946f8dd7aac8ca06dca5c43b6ee09787de9e5d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_nigrofasciatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_nigrofasciatus_specimen.jpg=edea58cd2541052f..., datasets/danio_nigrofasciatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_nigrofasciatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=2ffd9764fa0a9a43...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber formula. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: Danio pigment cells implement short-range activation and long-range inhibition and can form stripes or spots. | Parichy 2006: D. nigrofasciatus keeps a striped dorsum and a broken ventral field, unlike spotted D. margaritatus and striped D. rerio.; reconstructed_in_script: Explicit-Euler anisotropic Schnakenberg on a periodic cellular patch with dx set so analytical lambda_c equals 2.71e-05 m. | alpha_dorsal=6, alpha_ventral=1.15, break at 0.60 of flank height for the focal species; alpha=1.05 and alpha=8.5 for the chronospecies. | Trunk mask and composite painted onto the vendored Parichy photograph.; transfer_boundary: 27 µm is the catalog cellular wavelength, not a length resolved by the whole-body photograph. | alpha stands in for iridophore / Kcnj13 coupling; the script does not model those cells explicitly.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the organ-scale ~1 mm stripe spacing of slot 1203. | Does not claim the dorsoventral optical-density profile of the photograph is reproduced (profile Pearson r = 0.023). | Does not claim a second independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Score the alpha sweep (Spearman of anisotropy versus inverse horizontal gradient) and keep it on the comparison figure.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add the trunk gray KS statistic and the anterior-posterior holdout continuity gap, with references that are not copies of the measured values.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Assert the ablation (kinetics replaced by relaxation) and record the pattern-std / ablation-std ratio.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Re-run image fitness of the growth GIF against the Parichy specimen and write the per-loop fitness JSON only.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.759"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider on this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

